607	     * and, when numbered when opened (before numbering moved to settlement), takes the next number in the
608	     * sequence it would be numbered in (the sheet's, or while the sheet numbers by period, its due-by's
609	     * period's), its old number never given again (one not yet numbered gets none), loses any figure a statement bound it to (live again until its new person's next
610	     * statement), and is listed as its new person's newest claim. A SETTLED or VOID claim cannot move,
611	     * nor one due inside a closed period, nor one dated after its new person's retirement date.
